# Otterling agent rules

## Commits that will be AI-reviewed

When changing protections, filter-server, or Settings that touch filtering/VPN/Device Owner, add
`AI-REVIEW:` lines in the **commit body** explaining intent (especially unused-UI removals):

```text
AI-REVIEW: <what changed and why it is not a protection bypass>
```

The host release prompt includes `git log` for the cumulative range. Do not rely on the subject
line alone.

## Enforcement vs configuration UI

- **FAIL-worthy for the gate:** deleting/no-oping managers, VPN lockdown, fail-closed CONNECT,
  deny-list matching, Device Owner reapply, release cert pin.
- **Usually OK:** removing unused/superseded Settings composables when enforcement classes remain
  and a live path still covers the threat (e.g. VPN cloud filter instead of Private DNS UI).

## Self-lockout

- Do not move signing/publish into `.github/workflows`.
- Do not weaken `scripts/update_review_checklist.md` without a real strengthen (host pin is root).
- Emergency publish is root-only: `sudo otterling-release --force-publish 'reason'`.

## Scope reminders

- YouTube / banking apps: VPN bypass by default; Shorts/path rules via accessibility.
- Prefer editing `filter-server/` and `app/` with the live stack and phones in mind.
